{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537593-storyteller-vault-idea-craft-mini-booklets","id":1537593,"title":"Storyteller Vault Idea: Craft Mini-Booklets","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-06-17T20:03:45-07:00","id":1537593,"title":"Storyteller Vault Idea: Craft Mini-Booklets","content":"So I've been radio silent on my previous book project for a couple of month. Status report, it's almost done! Hoping to get the final proofing/edits done in the next couple of weeks and then submitted.<br /> <br /> Been thinking about possible future projects and this was a lot of work to be a mostly solo project (102 pages, so it's going to be a reasonably sized sourcebook), so I wondering if there was any interest in maybe mini booklets (like six to eight maybe) doing write ups on individual topics? For starters I was thinking of doing some optional Craft write ups. I had fun with the seven of those I ended up including in my book, and there is plenty of things I can build off of there. I'd probably end up making them pay what you want given their size.<br /> <br /> Does that sound interesting? Any requests on particular Crafts people would like to see?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T18:59:09-07:00","id":1538689,"title":"","content":"Still thinking about this as a future project. Putting together a list of possible Crafts. Several are the seed ideas for Crafts I included in my book:<br /> <br /> <b>The International Guild of Illusionists:</b> A inner circle of awakened stage magicians within a performers' guild more interested in wealth and fame than the ascension war.<br /> <b>The Sons of Liberty: </b>Remnants of the Craftmasons filtered through the American Revolution, then filtered again through Evangelical fundies and Reagan-era Republicans warping it further.<br /> <b>The Hieronymus Institute: </b>Old School Psionicists, combining psychic powers with electronic technomancy to boost them.<br /> <b>The Court of Phantasia: </b>Mages attuned to the Dreaming, forming a Fae like court structure. Might do a write up for a Spirit Variant Sphere for the Dreaming with them.<br /> <b>Watu wa Kesho:</b> Solar Punk Afro-futurists. I like the concept but admittedly need to do more research on this one.<br /> <b>Farandolae: </b>Freaky Biomancers. Like Parasite Eve level freaky.<br /> <br /> Additional Craft ideas include:<br /> <br /> <b>The Lotus Society: </b>Possibly courting with danger on this one. A rewrite of the Wu Keng. An off shoot of the Akashayana who became accepting of gender fluidity more quickly, and splintered off and diverged in practices long before the rest of the Tradition caught up with them on that. The Wu Lung hated them even more than the Akashayana, and much of the original back story is possibly just propaganda/fear mongering from them<br /> <b>The Horizon Council: </b>A version of the Council of Nine claiming to be from a still existing Concordia. Are they disembodied spirits like a Traditions' version of Threat Null? From another universe?<br /> <b>Artificial Genius: </b>A dark web group claiming to be able to artificially awaken volunteering sleepers. Easy power comes with consequences, of course.<br /> <b>Awakened Animals: </b>You thought only humans could awaken? While the road is even more difficult for animals, a rare few manage to somehow work it out enough to rival human Mages.<br /> <br /> Thoughts on these would be appreciated. My current idea is doing maybe 4 to 6 pages doing a general write, up with an additional 4 to 6 page of additional related info (Associated Variant or Minor Spheres, Backgrounds, Merits/Flaws, Foci, write of a location associated with, etc.). Haven't settled on a starting one yet.<br /> <br /> Thoughts/feedback are appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","user":"Becksworth","date":". 07-22-2024, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T19:21:38-07:00","id":1538690,"title":"","content":"Currently, Navalon holds the position closest to \u201cRight-wing American patriots\u201d. (If you read their entry in <b>The Operative's Dossier</b>, it sounds remarkably like a critique of the American Right.) They're not <i>quite </i>there; but they're awfully close. If you do the Sons of Liberty, you might want to put some serious thought into how they relate to Navalon. <br /> <br /> For what it's worth, I also see Navalon as a secret remnant of the Craftmasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T19:34:25-07:00","id":1538692,"title":"","content":"I thought Navalon were more a critique of Tories, which yeah is still pretty similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T23:42:12-07:00","id":1538707,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but the Craftmasons always smelled more like commies than anything else. They should be totalitarian neo marxists; the Craftmasons really have very little in common with evangelicals.<br /> <br /> Besides, if you want new crafts, you should focus on the new &quot;religions&quot; of the modern era. I would say they are the &quot;Techno Cult&quot;, exemplified in guys like Elon Musk, Mark Zuckerberg and others, that believe that technology will usher in an utopia, &quot;darwinists&quot; who are... Well, Nazis basically. Survival of the fittest style. Then there's the neo marxists. And of course, the christians. And Libertarians/Anarchocapitalists, who are sadly the smallest minority. But those are the religions of the West nowadays. That could be a start.<br /> <br /> And liberalism (classic liberalism, not what the commies today call &quot;liberalism&quot;) is pretty much dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-21T13:15:43-07:00","id":1538988,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm starting to like the Sons of Liberty as a Craftmasons offshoot. No one said a subculture needed to remain true to its forebears, or that people can't be hypocrites.<br /> <br /> I see the Sons of Liberty as the part of the Craftmasons who really got entrenched in the American political project. Slipping in a lot of sacred geometry and whatnot into the urban planning, architecture, and even documents and legal codes of the early US. You know, doing a lot of National Treasure stuff, like building secret underground vaults and leaving riddles throughout the land for other members (or potential members) to find.<br /> <br /> But once the Craftmasons were reorganized out of the Order of Reasons, during its transition to the Technocratic Union, the Sons of Liberty went even more underground. Splintering off into their own group, with their own goals of ensuring the survival of the US and its imperial dominance. Working in the shadows of American interests, and continuing to seed their works and designs into civic life.<br /> <br /> If I had to guess, I'd say their slip into Neocon, Evangelical thinking started during the Reagan era, when the Union made contact with them again. The Sons were an errant and quasi-mystical group, but they were discreet in their use of non-scientific Procedures. More importantly, the goals of the Sons aligned fairly well with the Union. Stability, subtle manipulation, and imperial hegemony. I think the Syndicate were the ones who made the most tempting offers. Using the Sons of Liberty as a tool in their efforts to increase the power of Capital in American life.<br /> <br /> And so, as one generation of Sons of Liberty made way for the next, both the big business and Evangelical mindset became engrained in the Craft. There's probably a lot of older or older style Sons who disliked the direction the Craft was moving. But they couldn't do anything about it, and their Union allies rewarded the new style (as the Evangelical movement was a powerful tool for the Technocracy).<br /> <br /> Fast forward to the turn of the millennium, and the Avatar Storm wrecked the Union's power structure. With the literal loss of Control, the Union couldn't maintain its hold on all its assets, or even knowledge of what all the pies they had fingers in. Inevitably, the need to consolidate power and maintain a strong front against the Traditions meant the Union couldn't keep tabs on everything or keep their &quot;client groups&quot; in line.<br /> <br /> So suddenly, the Sons of Liberty slipped their leash. The systems created by the Syndicate to funnel money to the Sons of Liberty remained in place. If anything, operating more vigorously, as big monied interests grew more entrenched within the Evangelical movement, and the reactionary politics it fostered. And you have yet another generation or two of Sons who grow up radicalized by right-wing thought leaders on the Internet. When they get recruited to the Craft, they're already deeply reactionary, if not full blown fascists.<br /> <br /> The Union thought they could tame this errant branch of their own lineage. Instead, at a moment of their weakness, the Sons of Liberty have metastasized into a real problem. In many ways a representation of the Conservative political and economic machine the Technocracy can no longer control. Movements that are exposing the lie of Capitalism, driving people to religious fervor, and tearing the political establishment apart.<br /> <br /> <br /> For inspirations, I might look at:<ul><li>National Treasure: as stated above. Great for old school mysteries and treasure hunt stories.</li> <li>Lovecraft Country: Similar to the National Treasure series, it has a number of treasure-hunting, dungeon delving aspects. With a healthy dose of reactionary politics. The overtly Lovecraftian elements can be scrubbed back if desired (though no one said members of the Sons can't have become corrupted by Umbral entities, or the Nephandi).</li> <li>Metal Gear Solid 2: Sons of Liberty: Naturally. It brings a very modern or near-future edge to the proceedings, which would work well for the current crop of &quot;America First&quot; nationalists that interweaves tech bro obsessions. The use of technology, bent to the ends of bilking people out of money and rearranging the financial and social order to the control of wealthy assholes. In effect, tech bro Sons of Liberty try to weave their Craft's sacred geometry into the architecture of our digital existence, just as their forebears did with literal architecture.</li> <li>Bioshock Infinite: the Sons of Liberty sound like they would heavily channel the vibe of Columbia. With their tech bro nonsense as established above, they might even want to build it. At the very least, they worship the Founding Fathers as saints, and would gladly throw robots with their faces on them at their enemies (Paradox permitting).</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-21T17:15:06-07:00","id":1538997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Becksworth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537593-storyteller-vault-idea-craft-mini-booklets?p=1538689#post1538689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Farandolae: </b>Freaky Biomancers. Like Parasite Eve level freaky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not much to say other than I love the name. I never see anyone reference L\u2019Engle books other than Wrinkle in Time. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T02:34:13-07:00","id":1539006,"title":"","content":"Frankly, given the original Sons of Liberty were left-wing radicals, I'd rather see them as frustrated small d democrats fighting the brutal influence of the NWO and the Syndicate. Treating any reference to the American Revolutionary War as fascist is pushing America in a reactionary political direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T10:20:09-07:00","id":1539040,"title":"","content":"Like Bluecho mentioned, hypocrisy was a theme I was looking to work with for the Sons of Liberty. Yeah, for their time many of the American founders were pretty left leaning, but tell that to the people who dress up as them.<br /> <br /> In any case, they're not the first group I'm going to tackle (and likely not the 2nd for the matter). To start I think I'm tackling the Guild of Illusionists, as it's the most fleshed out in my head. Plus I just got back from Vegas and it's fresh on my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T13:44:39-07:00","id":1539242,"title":"","content":"My interpretation of the Sons of Liberty presumes that whatever &quot;Old School&quot; current remains in the Craft, that cares about revolutionary politics and the simple art of Sacred Geometry, has been overshadowed by a reactionary movement that mirrors the one found in Sleeper culture. In a setting like Mage where every religious movement seems to have a practitioner among the Awakened, it only makes sense that a group would subscribe to the &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_civil_religion\" target=\"_blank\">American Civil Religion</a>&quot; seen in the US that worships the Founders as prophets and which holds America's symbols, documents, locations, and institutions as sacred.<br /> <br /> In essence, the belief in the American Experiment found in the original Sons of Liberty has ossified into a belief in the sacredness of America. Arguably, this would have begun in the 19th century, and only became more rigid, conservative, and ultimately reactionary in the years since. This adherence to the institutions of the US, more than anything, attracted the Technocracy to the Sons of Liberty, and made them useful pawns.<br /> <br /> Naturally, I don't want to contend there AREN'T members of the Craft that hold to its original values. Only that these are the minority, as modern adherents of the American Civil Religion flood the ranks of the Craft and gain primacy through sheer numbers and political clout. Such recruits are a high control group, as the kind of person attracted to this side of the Craft is more zealous about the Civil Religion than normal people (otherwise, they wouldn't get involved in a highly secretive, esoteric group). Whereas the pool of academics, architects, code-breakers, and activists that are attracted to the &quot;Orthodox&quot; camp have largely remained static. (You have to both really want to dedicate yourself to the particular brand of sacred geometry, AND not get swept up in the high energy, radicalizing wings of the Craft).<br /> <br /> The ones that tow the line of Evangelicalism and American Fascism also tend to get alloted the most funding from the Craft's big business sponsors, both because those corporate interests personally agree with it, and by design of the Syndicate when they put those revenue streams in place. Meaning the reactionary subset has the most funding for projects, recruitment, and &quot;defense&quot;.<br /> <br /> PCs outside this Craft might encounter the &quot;moderate&quot;/&quot;Orthodox&quot; parts on occasion, in an academic manner. Or at worst, when competing for resources or when they disrupt infrastructure put in place centuries ago, that the &quot;Old Guard&quot; want to protect. Meanwhile, the reactionary, Evangelical part of the Craft is more likely to be faced as <i>Antagonists</i>. Since they have both their own resources, those funneled (if only by automation) to them by the Syndicate, and groups of Sleepers/hunters that despise non-standard (read: Evangelical) religious practices or left-wing political causes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-19T09:00:20-07:00","id":1551768,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/526647/Modern-Crafts-Volume-One\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/pr...fts-Volume-One</a><br /> <br /> Alright, there's was few delays getting here, but Volume One of Modern Crafts is available now. I think I'm going to break from this concept for now. Between this, Book of Spheres and Warlock I've done about 40 sect write ups in the span of a year, so I want to on something different for a bit. I still want to do at least a Volume Two at some point, but not immediately after Volume One.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T16:27:41-08:00","id":1557930,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the thread necro, but I got a Volume Two now available:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/en/product/554581/modern-crafts-volume-two\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/en...fts-volume-two</a><br /> <br /> I also made a discount link for Volume One if anyone is curious about that one still.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?discountId=9722e774f3\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/br...tId=9722e774f3</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}